# No deprecated APIs

New and changed code must not call an API Matplotlib has deprecated. Before finishing, search the diff for `@_api.deprecated`, `.. deprecated::`, `warn_deprecated`, and `MatplotlibDeprecationWarning`.

Use the replacement named in the deprecation warning. Do not add a public wrapper that calls the deprecated name.

```python
# ❌ BAD — matplotlib.transforms.nonsingular was deprecated in 3.11
from matplotlib.transforms import nonsingular
vmin, vmax = nonsingular(vmin, vmax)

# ✅ GOOD — call the replacement
from matplotlib.transforms import _nonsingular
vmin, vmax = _nonsingular(vmin, vmax)
```

A test may call a deprecated API only to lock the warning, and it must assert that warning:

```python
with pytest.warns(mpl.MatplotlibDeprecationWarning, match="deprecated"):
    fig.number = 2
```

Do not silence `MatplotlibDeprecationWarning` with a blanket filter.
